  "body": "## What changed\nThe maintainer said in chat on 2026-11-22: \"PR's with merge-ready cannot have needs-rework at the same time..\"\n\nNew rule, written with the same words in each place:\n- `merge-ready` and `needs-rework` are never on the same PR.\n- The person or agent that sets one removes the other in the same `gh pr edit` call, with one comment that says why.\n- If two collaborators disagree on the same head, `needs-rework` stays and `merge-ready` is removed. An open change request wins. The comment goes to the collaborator who set `merge-ready`.\n- `/merge-ready` never offers a PR with `needs-rework`.\n- `conflicts` stays an add-alongside label.\n\nFiles:\n- `AGENTS.md`: rule \"Only collaborators' reviews count\" (the disagreement item is replaced by three items) and one line below the \"Review labels\" table.\n- `.claude/skills/merge-ready/SKILL.md`: the disagreement paragraph is replaced by the rule. A PR with `needs-rework` is not offered.\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`: the label steps say \"in the same `gh pr edit` call\". The disagreement paragraph is replaced by the rule.\n- `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md`: step 8 sets one label and removes the other in one call.\n- `.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/SKILL.md`: the DELTA verdict `needs-rework` removes `merge-ready` in the same call.\n\nNo file under `xtask/` pins the old text. No test changes.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo build and no test run. This is a text change in process files.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3382\n",
